description:
The symbols a change affects and the tests to run. With no symbol, symbol_id, or file, it reads the uncommitted git changes. Text output supports bounded per-section pages and optional low-signal import, variable, parameter, field, property, module, and namespace rows. Each call reads the current index; keep the same project_root and filter, and restart at offset 0 after index changes. The page limit is at most 200; discovery stops at 200 rows and larger offsets return no rows.

Pass project_root, the absolute path of the project or git worktree you work in, on every call. Call file_skeleton on a folder or a file you do not know. Before you change a symbol, call get_symbol_context for its body, callers, tests, and types. Read the file you will edit. Use lookup_symbol for a name or a concept, and find_references, not grep, for its uses. After you edit, call check_edit before you say the change is done; blast_radius() lists the tests of the whole diff.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__code_kb__blast_radius(args: {
  // Hops (default: 2, at most 5).
  depth?: number;
  // File path.
  file?: string;
  // Include low-signal import, variable, parameter, field, property, module, and namespace impact rows (default: false).
  include_low_signal?: boolean;
  // Per section (default: 20).
  limit?: number;
  // Text page offset in the test and impact sections (default: 0). restart at offset 0 after an index change. Larger offsets return no rows after the 200-row discovery ceiling.
  offset?: number;
  // Absolute path of the project or git worktree you work in. Change it when you move to another.
  project_root: string;
  // Symbol name.
  symbol?: string;
  // The id from lookup_symbol; pass one of this or symbol.
  symbol_id?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

After you edit: the symbols whose shape changed against the session base (or base, or HEAD) and every site of each that your diff did not reach. Run it before you say a change is done. Text output supports bounded pages for each folded section; each call reads the current index, keep the same project_root and base, and restart at offset 0 after index changes. The default page size is 12; page limit is at most 200 and offset may extend beyond 200.

Pass project_root, the absolute path of the project or git worktree you work in, on every call. Call file_skeleton on a folder or a file you do not know. Before you change a symbol, call get_symbol_context for its body, callers, tests, and types. Read the file you will edit. Use lookup_symbol for a name or a concept, and find_references, not grep, for its uses. After you edit, call check_edit before you say the change is done; blast_radius() lists the tests of the whole diff.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__code_kb__check_edit(args: {
  // Git revision to compare with (default: the session base, else HEAD).
  base?: string;
  // Page size per folded section (default: 12 when paging is requested; maximum 200).
  limit?: number;
  // Text page offset per folded section (default: 0). restart at offset 0 after an index change. The offset may exceed 200.
  offset?: number;
  // Absolute path of the project or git worktree you work in. Change it when you move to another.
  project_root: string;
