Callers of a symbol: every indexed site with its name, each labeled proven, likely, unresolved, or excluded by its evidence, plus a whole-word text count that accounts for every line of the name. A field, property, variable, or constant lists its writes first. Use instead of rg or grep on a name. Callees: the calls a symbol makes. Pass file_path or a qualified name for a common name. Text reports support bounded per-section pages; each call reads the current index, keep the same project_root and filter, and restart at offset 0 after index changes. Page limit is at most 200; offset may extend beyond 200.

Pass project_root, the absolute path of the project or git worktree you work in, on every call. Call file_skeleton on a folder or a file you do not know. Before you change a symbol, call get_symbol_context for its body, callers, tests, and types. Read the file you will edit. Use lookup_symbol for a name or a concept, and find_references, not grep, for its uses. After you edit, call check_edit before you say the change is done; blast_radius() lists the tests of the whole diff.

